# Local Dev (No Docker)

This project runs **without Docker** in local development. Do **not** use `pnpm dev` (it uses Docker Compose).

## Control script (required)

Use the project script instead of ad-hoc shell commands for Redis / API / Celery / frontend:

```bash
./scripts/local-dev.sh restart   # preferred after .env or cookie changes
./scripts/local-dev.sh status    # health-check everything
./scripts/local-dev.sh stop
./scripts/local-dev.sh start
```

pnpm aliases:

```bash
pnpm local:restart
pnpm local:status
pnpm local:stop
pnpm local:start
```

## After config changes

Always **`restart`** (not just API) when changing:

- `.env` / `packages/hermes-api/.env`
- `HERMES_COOKIES_JSON` or cookie JSON files under `packages/hermes-api/cookies/`

Celery loads settings at process start. Restarting only uvicorn leaves downloads broken.

## Ports / URLs

- Frontend: http://127.0.0.1:5174 (5173 may be used by other apps)
- API: http://127.0.0.1:8000
- API docs: http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs
- Logs: `/tmp/hermes-api.log`, `/tmp/hermes-celery.log`, `/tmp/hermes-app.log`

## Cookies

- Editable JSON (not hardcoded): `packages/hermes-api/cookies/youtube.json`, `tiktok.json`
- Env: `HERMES_COOKIES_JSON=./cookies/youtube.json,./cookies/tiktok.json`
- Files are gitignored; examples are `*.json.example`

## TikTok yt-dlp knobs (TikTok-only by default)

```bash
HERMES_YTDLP_IMPERSONATE=chrome
HERMES_YTDLP_IMPERSONATE_SITES=tiktok
HERMES_YTDLP_USER_AGENT=Mozilla/5.0
```

Docs: `docs/LOCAL_DEV.md`, `docs/CONFIGURATION.md`
